{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.83681efd04","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-361","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Merrow Tunnel is in southern Norway. It opened in 1902.</li><li>Its length is 55 kilometers.</li><li>The Sable Tunnel is in southern Brazil. It opened in 2006.</li><li>Its length is 43 kilometers.</li><li>Both are tunnels that pass under a mountain range.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize how the length of the two tunnels differs.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The length of the Merrow Tunnel (55 kilometers) is greater than that of the Sable Tunnel (43 kilometers).","The Merrow Tunnel, which is in southern Norway, is one of several tunnels that pass under a mountain range.","The Merrow Tunnel opened in 1902, while the Sable Tunnel opened in 2006.","Both the Merrow Tunnel and the Sable Tunnel are tunnels that pass under a mountain range."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It compares the length of both tunnels. The other choices describe a similarity, a difference in date, or only one tunnel."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.556f5c8cde","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-365","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Sable Tower is in western Kenya. It was completed in 2019.</li><li>Its height is 431 meters.</li><li>The Pembrook Tower is in central Spain. It was completed in 2003.</li><li>Its height is 382 meters.</li><li>Both are observation towers open to the public.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast when the two towers were completed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Both the Sable Tower and the Pembrook Tower are observation towers open to the public.","The height of the Sable Tower (431 meters) is greater than that of the Pembrook Tower (382 meters).","The Sable Tower was completed in 2019, while the Pembrook Tower was completed in 2003.","The Sable Tower is in western Kenya, and the Pembrook Tower is in central Spain."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It gives both dates and contrasts them. The other choices compare size or location, or describe a similarity."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.604218a755","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-368","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Quarry Tunnel is in eastern Australia. It opened in 1893.</li><li>Its length is 17 kilometers.</li><li>The Cresthill Tunnel is in northern Chile. It opened in 1917.</li><li>Its length is 5 kilometers.</li><li>Both are railway tunnels.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast when the two tunnels opened.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Both the Quarry Tunnel and the Cresthill Tunnel are railway tunnels.","The Quarry Tunnel is in eastern Australia, and the Cresthill Tunnel is in northern Chile.","The Quarry Tunnel opened in 1893, while the Cresthill Tunnel opened in 1917.","The length of the Quarry Tunnel (17 kilometers) is greater than that of the Cresthill Tunnel (5 kilometers)."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It gives both dates and contrasts them. The other choices compare size or location, or describe a similarity."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.e5f68d8e43","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-380","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Orla Observatory is in northern India. It began operating in 1966.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 10 meters.</li><li>The Cresthill Observatory is in eastern Australia. It began operating in 2010.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 7 meters.</li><li>Both are radio observatories.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize how the main telescope's mirror diameter of the two observatorys differs.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The main telescope's mirror diameter of the Orla Observatory (10 meters) is greater than that of the Cresthill Observatory (7 meters).","The Orla Observatory began operating in 1966, while the Cresthill Observatory began operating in 2010.","The Orla Observatory, which is in northern India, is one of several radio observatories.","Both the Orla Observatory and the Cresthill Observatory are radio observatories."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It compares the main telescope's mirror diameter of both observatorys. The other choices describe a similarity, a difference in date, or only one observatory."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.216302bd01","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-392","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Glenrock Tower is in western Kenya. It was completed in 2018.</li><li>Its height is 488 meters.</li><li>The Quarry Tower is in eastern Poland. It was completed in 1922.</li><li>Its height is 101 meters.</li><li>Both are towers built mainly of steel.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast when the two towers were completed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Both the Glenrock Tower and the Quarry Tower are towers built mainly of steel.","The height of the Glenrock Tower (488 meters) is greater than that of the Quarry Tower (101 meters).","The Glenrock Tower is in western Kenya, and the Quarry Tower is in eastern Poland.","The Glenrock Tower was completed in 2018, while the Quarry Tower was completed in 1922."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It gives both dates and contrasts them. The other choices compare size or location, or describe a similarity."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.71bc7087f7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-398","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Glenrock Tunnel is in southern Norway. It opened in 1913.</li><li>Its length is 22 kilometers.</li><li>The Brookhaven Tunnel is in southern Brazil. It opened in 1974.</li><li>Its length is 14 kilometers.</li><li>Both are tunnels that pass under a mountain range.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast when the two tunnels opened.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The length of the Glenrock Tunnel (22 kilometers) is greater than that of the Brookhaven Tunnel (14 kilometers).","Both the Glenrock Tunnel and the Brookhaven Tunnel are tunnels that pass under a mountain range.","The Glenrock Tunnel is in southern Norway, and the Brookhaven Tunnel is in southern Brazil.","The Glenrock Tunnel opened in 1913, while the Brookhaven Tunnel opened in 1974."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It gives both dates and contrasts them. The other choices compare size or location, or describe a similarity."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.b71894d082","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-399","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Northam National Park is in western Scotland. It was established in 2018.</li><li>Its area is 6,246 square kilometers.</li><li>Alder National Park is in northern India. It was established in 2013.</li><li>Its area is 5,765 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are parks that protect coastal wetlands.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between Northam National Park and Alder National Park.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Northam National Park was established in 2018, while Alder National Park was established in 2013.","Northam National Park is in western Scotland, and Alder National Park is in northern India.","The area of Northam National Park (6,246 square kilometers) is greater than that of Alder National Park (5,765 square kilometers).","Both Northam National Park and Alder National Park are parks that protect coastal wetlands."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. Only this choice describes something the two share. The others present differences (in size, date, or location)."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.c4eede9354","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-1","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Omar Brennan is a marine biologist.</li><li>Brennan wanted to find out whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.</li><li>Brennan recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.</li><li>Brennan found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.</li><li>Brennan concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Brennan found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.","Brennan concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.","To investigate the question, Brennan recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.","Marine biologist Omar Brennan set out to learn whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.0e96cd590a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-17","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Nakamura is a psychologist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.</li><li>Nakamura had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.</li><li>Nakamura found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Nakamura concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.","To investigate the question, Nakamura had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.","Psychologist Zara Nakamura set out to learn whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.","Nakamura found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.fa684f463e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-18","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Diego Haddad is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Haddad grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Haddad found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Haddad concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Haddad grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.","Haddad found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.","Haddad concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","Agricultural scientist Diego Haddad set out to learn whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.6090508acf","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-23","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Nakamura is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Nakamura grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Nakamura found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Nakamura grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.","Agricultural scientist Nadia Nakamura set out to learn whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.","Nakamura concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","Nakamura found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.d3316ba6b6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-30","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Yara Nakamura is an entomologist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.</li><li>Nakamura set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.</li><li>Nakamura found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Nakamura concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.","Entomologist Yara Nakamura set out to learn whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.","To investigate the question, Nakamura set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.","Nakamura found that bees visited the blue feeders most often."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.1fec25d69e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-32","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Omar Asante is an entomologist.</li><li>Asante wanted to find out whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.</li><li>Asante set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.</li><li>Asante found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.</li><li>Asante concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Asante set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.","Asante found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.","Entomologist Omar Asante set out to learn whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.","Asante concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.655d5829e9","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-35","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Solberg is an entomologist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.</li><li>Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.</li><li>Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.</li><li>Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.","To investigate the question, Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.","Entomologist Dmitri Solberg set out to learn whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.","Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.49b6de92d2","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-40","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Imani Delacroix is a sociologist.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.</li><li>Delacroix surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.</li><li>Delacroix found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Delacroix found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.","Sociologist Imani Delacroix set out to learn whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.","Delacroix concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.","To investigate the question, Delacroix surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.c02c7ff5ec","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-41","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Varga is a sociologist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.</li><li>Varga surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.</li><li>Varga found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.</li><li>Varga concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Sociologist Tomás Varga set out to learn whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.","Varga concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.","Varga found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.","To investigate the question, Varga surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.41e5a5c212","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-59","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Haddad is a zoologist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.</li><li>Haddad gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.</li><li>Haddad found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.</li><li>Haddad concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Haddad found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.","To investigate the question, Haddad gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.","Zoologist Ingrid Haddad set out to learn whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.","Haddad concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.699124f7e3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-74","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Moreau is an economist.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.</li><li>Moreau tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.</li><li>Moreau found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.</li><li>Moreau concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Moreau concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","Moreau found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.","Economist Felipe Moreau set out to learn whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.","To investigate the question, Moreau tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.5cf7f3ce50","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-85","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Imani Oyelaran is an urban planner.</li><li>Oyelaran wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Oyelaran measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Oyelaran found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Oyelaran concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Oyelaran measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.","Oyelaran found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.","Oyelaran concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.","Urban planner Imani Oyelaran set out to learn whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.3639fa7f24","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-95","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Quintero is a hydrologist.</li><li>Quintero wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Quintero compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Quintero found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Quintero concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Hydrologist Sofia Quintero set out to learn whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.","To investigate the question, Quintero compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.","Quintero found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.","Quintero concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.1dfd77fc8d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-101","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Oyelaran is an education researcher.</li><li>Oyelaran wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Oyelaran had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Oyelaran found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Oyelaran concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Oyelaran concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","Oyelaran found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.","Education researcher Jonas Oyelaran set out to learn whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.","To investigate the question, Oyelaran had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.75cb47ca79","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-102","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Mbeki is a chemist.</li><li>Mbeki wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Mbeki placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Mbeki found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Mbeki concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Mbeki placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.","Mbeki found that most samples broke apart within four months.","Mbeki concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.","Chemist Nadia Mbeki set out to learn whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.47cdf944ed","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-103","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Chen Delacroix is a chemist.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Delacroix placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Delacroix found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Delacroix placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.","Delacroix concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.","Delacroix found that most samples broke apart within four months.","Chemist Chen Delacroix set out to learn whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.0a2203ab18","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-110","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Mensah is a primatologist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Mensah observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Mensah found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Mensah concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mensah found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.","Mensah concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.","To investigate the question, Mensah observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.","Primatologist Priya Mensah set out to learn whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.168d5c8f13","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-122","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Lindqvist is an ornithologist.</li><li>Lindqvist wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Lindqvist measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Lindqvist found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Lindqvist concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Lindqvist concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","To investigate the question, Lindqvist measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.","Ornithologist Ingrid Lindqvist set out to learn whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.","Lindqvist found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.9bae586501","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-131","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Samuel Novak is a public health researcher.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.","Public health researcher Samuel Novak set out to learn whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.","Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","To investigate the question, Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.6bc9242785","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-132","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Amara Okafor is an archaeologist.</li><li>Okafor wanted to find out whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages.</li><li>Okafor analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.</li><li>Okafor found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.</li><li>Okafor concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Archaeologist Amara Okafor set out to learn whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages.","Okafor found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.","To investigate the question, Okafor analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.","Okafor concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.ef60477f19","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-140","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Hana Novak is a neuroscientist.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.</li><li>Novak scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.</li><li>Novak found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.</li><li>Novak concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Novak found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.","Novak concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.","Neuroscientist Hana Novak set out to learn whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.","To investigate the question, Novak scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.ff0b1c954d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-144","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Castellano is a marine ecologist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.</li><li>Castellano fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.</li><li>Castellano found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.</li><li>Castellano concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Castellano concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.","Marine ecologist Ravi Castellano set out to learn whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.","To investigate the question, Castellano fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.","Castellano found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.ca3780df1e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-147","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Amara Haddad is a marine ecologist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.</li><li>Haddad fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.</li><li>Haddad found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.</li><li>Haddad concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Haddad found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.","Marine ecologist Amara Haddad set out to learn whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.","To investigate the question, Haddad fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.","Haddad concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.6b4e63aea6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-154","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Mensah is a climate scientist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Mensah compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Mensah found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Mensah concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Climate scientist Ingrid Mensah set out to learn whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.","To investigate the question, Mensah compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.","Mensah found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.","Mensah concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.c3b2e902b6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-154","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Mensah is a climate scientist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Mensah compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Mensah found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Mensah concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Climate scientist Ingrid Mensah set out to learn whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.","Mensah concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","Mensah found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.","To investigate the question, Mensah compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.b5d1cbb449","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-159","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Samuel Delacroix is a behavioral economist.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.</li><li>Delacroix moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.</li><li>Delacroix found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Delacroix concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.","Delacroix found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.","To investigate the question, Delacroix moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.","Behavioral economist Samuel Delacroix set out to learn whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.258abc05ce","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-160","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Asante is a behavioral economist.</li><li>Asante wanted to find out whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.</li><li>Asante moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.</li><li>Asante found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.</li><li>Asante concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Asante concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.","To investigate the question, Asante moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.","Asante found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.","Behavioral economist Jonas Asante set out to learn whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.8378fbc4fa","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-163","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Lindqvist is a veterinary scientist.</li><li>Lindqvist wanted to find out whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.</li><li>Lindqvist played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.</li><li>Lindqvist found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.</li><li>Lindqvist concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Lindqvist played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.","Veterinary scientist Jonas Lindqvist set out to learn whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.","Lindqvist found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.","Lindqvist concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."}
